# Server structure

Read `docs/BACKEND_STRUCTURE.md` and `docs/CODE_CONVENTIONS.md` before adding or changing a server resource.

Request flow: component → Redux → Express route → controller → service → repository → Prisma.

- Files use the plural resource name: `users_controller.ts`, `users_service.ts`, `users_repository.ts`, `users_schema.ts`.
- Operations use snake_case, action plus singular entity, and the same name on the controller and service: `list_user`, `create_user`, `list_by_id_user`, `update_user`, `delete_user`.
- Routes own URLs, access middleware, and rate limiters. Controllers translate HTTP. Services own business conditions. Repositories own Prisma queries.
- Each controller handler has its own `try`/`catch`. Do not add a shared `failure()` helper. New catalog controllers pass `req.body` through and do not add field parsers.
- `src/server/schema` and `src/types` stay separate. Do not import one from the other. Components and Redux do not import `src/server` or generated Prisma code.
